            <ArticleTitle>Sleep medicine is coming of age in military medicine : Report from the Military Health System Research Symposium (2017) in Kissimmee, Florida.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11325-017-1595-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In August 2017, the US Military Health System held its sixth annual Research Symposium for medical researchers from the US Army, Navy, Air Force, and Public Health Service. The symposium provides a collaborative environment for academia, industry, and military researchers who address advancement in areas of Combat Casualty Care, Military Operational Medicine, Clinical and Rehabilitative Medicine, and Military Infectious Diseases. This year, Sleep Medicine received substantial attention with presentations scattered throughout the program, poster presentations as well as a scheduled breakout session with podium presentations. A brief description of the breakout session follows.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
